			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿",
				97,
				104
			],
			"Message": "chore(Output): Remove Configuration build directory\n\nDelete the entire Configuration directory from Output element. These build configuration files (ESBuild configs, plugins, polyfills, service modules, tsconfigs) were intermediate artifacts that should be regenerated from source during the build process rather than persisted in the Output tree.\n\nThis reduces confusion between source build configs and output artifacts, and ensures the Output directory contains only the final bundled JS artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime.",
			"SHA": "d0b23daeb49a7f2516c8b520bafccc22be4cc44f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T18:46:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add playwright.__initialize stub and improve disposition telemetry\n\nAdd `__initialize` to the playwright stub to handle `PlaywrightChannelClient` constructor posting protocol version negotiation. This surfaced as `disposition=drift` in previous boot logs. Also add explicit `setExtensionGalleryManifest` stub for extension gallery metadata seeding.\n\nReplace the binary `present=true/false` stub-hit logging with three-state disposition: `value` (stub has real payload), `noop` (stub key intentionally undefined like telemetryAppender.log), and `drift` (channel stubbed but command missing - needs investigation). This helps developers distinguish between \"method intentionally returns undefined\" vs \"stub key missing from object\".",
			"SHA": "b7dc4a7243028788d13edcd2f6f19fda6fc96eef"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:24:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add localGit routing and Batch 6 IPC channel stubs\n\nAdd the `localGit` channel route mapping to route VS Code's built-in Git extension IPC to Mountain's `git:*` subprocess handlers. This fixes the SourceControl panel hanging forever at load with `InvokeMountain(\"undefined:exec\")`.\n\nAdd Batch 6 medium-priority channel stubs for services stock VS Code exposes via the shared process that Land doesn't implement: test results storage, profile storage listener, checksum service, language packs, user data sync utilities/machines/resource provider, custom endpoint telemetry, tunnel services, web content extraction, playwright automation, and V8 profiling.\n\nAlso enhance `InvokeMountain` with per-invoke timing telemetry logged to the `tauri-invoke` tag, capturing round-trip duration including Tauri transport overhead. This differentiates slow Rust handlers (large `ipc done t_ns`) from starved webview channels (large `tauri-invoke elapsed_ms` but small Rust-side time).",
			"SHA": "a79767ad78cd9de37302e3fddb58e95cffd93e79"
		}
	],
